WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
 hello and welcome to another walkthrough for Computer Architecture for Everybody.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.040
 So in this walkthrough we are going to walk through the assignment of building a half adder.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.700
 So in the instructions for this half adder we are seeing the reference diagram.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:20.600
 So it's really nothing more than exclusive OR at the top and an AND at the bottom with the input of A and B and a sum and carry as the output.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:25.040
 The output of the exclusive OR is the sum and the output of the AND is the carry.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.480
 And we just run the inputs to both of the gates and away we go.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.180
 So I can just leave this up and so let's just go ahead and start putting this in.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:40.040
 Input, put place an input, place another input, let's place an exclusive OR.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:45.880
 And again remember these are just transistors, they're just kind of in functional block diagrams that are useful to us.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:49.440
 And then let's do an AND, place an AND.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:56.740
 And then wire up the inputs to the two inputs of the exclusive OR, oops, there we go.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:02.980
 That input goes to the other input to the exclusive OR, then the input to the AND, both of them go to the AND.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:09.680
 I mean and really what we're doing is we're just making the truth table work, then we need an output.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:21.280
 The sum output is the exclusive OR and then the carry out output is the AND.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:27.220
 So both are true, so one plus one equals two, so that's a zero one, that's two.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.780
 So let's go ahead and tag these correctly.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:37.140
 Let's tag the top one sum, let's tag the bottom one carry.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:40.520
 Oh, wait a sec, are we supposed to call it carry or carry out?

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:46.280
 C out, so we're supposed to call that one C out, so the reference diagram is not quite right.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:52.240
 That's okay, C-O-U-T, that reference diagram was just from the lecture, so we got C out.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:02:03.120
 And then we have, let's go back to the specs, got inputs of A and B, let's tag the input of A, tag the input of B.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:13.080
 Okay, so we have one plus one equals zero carry the one, zero plus zero is zero carry the zero, zero plus one is one carry the zero.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.120
 So this looks like it's working pretty well.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.580
 You can take a look at the truth table, right?

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:26.840
 So this truth table is zero of A and a one of B and the sum should be one and the carry out should be one and so it looks good.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:30.780
 So you can sort of verify this, you can manually manipulate the one and the zero.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.780
 It's a good way to remember how half adders work, so let's go ahead and start the grading.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:40.620
 It says we got all required components are properly labeled, we got an A and a B and a sum and a C out.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:43.940
 And then we got an XOR and AND gate, that's good.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:51.540
 And now it's going to do all the four truth tables, zero zero turns into A of zero, B of zero turns into sum of zero, C out of zero.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:55.220
 A of zero, B of one turns into a sum of one and a C out of zero.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:59.580
 A of one and B of zero is sum of one, C out is zero.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.280
 And then we finish and away we go.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:11.120
 So I hope this little walkthrough of how to do a half adder assignment in the gates layout tool for Computer Architecture for Everybody has been helpful to you.

